## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to engineer a practical, scalable evaluation system for real-world multilingual policy assistants operating under complex brand-specific constraints with live documentation dependencies.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual policy alignment across distinct brand ecosystems
- Versioned, source-grounded citation verification and tracking
- Cross-brand policy conflict detection and temporal drift analysis
- Lightweight evaluation datasets with granular per-claim scoring mechanisms

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example citation validation function
function validateCitationCurrentness(claim, policyIndex) {
  const citation = claim?.citation;
  const policy = policyIndex.find(p => p.id === citation?.policyId);
  return policy && policy.version === citation?.version && policy.isActive;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Microsoft tests understanding of tokenization trade-offs and attention mechanisms in multilingual contexts - critical for products like Bing Chat and Azure AI services.

## Expected Answer
Strong candidates discuss: 1) Byte-Pair Encoding with language-specific merges, 2) Vocabulary size vs token count trade-offs, 3) Adding language ID tokens, 4) Attention modifications like language-aware positional encoding or cross-lingual attention heads.

## Code Example
```typescript
// Custom tokenizer with language-aware merges
class MultilingualTokenizer {
  vocabulary: Map<string, number>
  languageMerges: Map<string, string[]>

  tokenize(text: string, lang: string): number[] {
    const tokens = []
    const merges = this.languageMerges.get(lang) || []
    // Apply language-specific BPE merges
    return this.applyBPE(text, merges)
  }
}

// Language-aware attention modification
class LanguageAwareAttention {
  forward(x: Tensor, langIds: Tensor): Tensor {
    const attention = this.multiHeadAttention(x)
    const langBias = this.getLanguageBias(langIds)
    return attention + langBias
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle rare characters or emojis in the vocabulary?
- What metrics would you use to evaluate tokenizer efficiency?
- How does this approach scale to 50+ languages?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to translate a real-world costing task into a reproducible, beginner-friendly LangChain planning flow that uses tool orchestration and simple arithmetic.

## Key Concepts

- Tool selection and orchestration
- Planning vs. execution, simple ReAct-like flow
- Cost estimation: hourly to monthly, data transfer edges, taxes
- Fallbacks for missing pricing data

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal planning snippet illustrating tool invocation
async function planCost(query){
  const prices = await pricingApi.getPrices({services:["EC2","RDS","CloudFront"], instance:"t4g.medium"});
  const monthly = prices.ec2 * 730 + prices.rds * 730 + prices.cloudfront * 730;
  return monthly;
}
```

